===Etymology 2===
From {{inh|en|enm|rejoynen}}, from {{der|en|frm||rejoin-}} (stem of {{m|frm|rejoindre}}, from {{m|frm|re-|t=again}} + {{m|frm|joindre|t=to join}}).<ref>{{R:MED Online|entry=rejoinen|pos=v|id=MED36589}}</ref><ref>{{R:OED Online|pos=''v.''{{sup|1}}|noformat=1|id=1104735065}}</ref> {{surf|en|re-|join}}. {{doublet|en|rejoinder}}.

====Verb====
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|archaic}} To state in reply.
#* {{RQ:Falkner Moonfleet|page=44|passage="Be careful what you do," '''rejoined''' another man's voice that I did not know, "lest someone see you digging, and scent us out."}}
# {{lb|en|archaic|intransitive}} To answer to a reply.
# {{lb|en|legal|intransitive}} To answer, as the defendant to the [[plaintiff]]'s replication.
# {{lb|en|patent law|non-standard}} <i>in US patent law</i> To re-insert a patent claim, typically after allowance of a patent application, applied to patent claims that had been withdrawn from examination under a restriction requirement, based on [[rejoinder]] {{lb|en|patent law}}.

